q("T-T05","test","table","For summation global public goods, what recommendations appear in Table 3.1?","Grants and loans to foster fairness, plus multilateral institutions to monitor and track contributions.",[(91,"Summation ... Grants and loans are needed to foster fairness and multilateral institutions are needed to monitor and track contributions","table")]),
q("T-T06","test","table","What is Switzerland's 2022 HDI and PHDI in Table 7, and what percentage difference from HDI does the table show?","HDI 0.967; PHDI 0.826; difference −14.6%.",[(315,"1 Switzerland 0.967 0.826 14.6","table")]),
q("T-I01","test","image_diagram","In Figure 4.1, identify the two circular nodes and explain their relationship.","Behavioural change and institutional/policy change influence one another; the interaction is mutually dependent and based on social choice procedures.",[(116,"Behavioural change ... Institutional and policy change ... Interactions are mutually dependent","diagram")]),
q("T-I02","test","image_diagram","Reading Figure 2.4 as a flow diagram, what path links interdependence shocks to electoral support for populism?","Shocks/human-development losses change beliefs and attitudes; this shapes policy preferences and leader preferences/programmes, culminating in electoral support for populism.",[(67,"Mismanaged interdependence → shocks ... Human development losses ... Changes in beliefs ... Electoral outcomes: Support for populism","diagram")]),
q("T-I03","test","image_diagram","Name two United Kingdom government organizations labeled on the Figure 4.2 world map.","Examples include BEIS (UK) and HMCTS (UK). Other correct examples include FCDO, HMRC, DfT, DfE, Ofgem or BIT, each labeled UK.",[(124,"Figure 4.2 map labels include BEIS (UK), HMCTS (UK), FCDO (UK), HMRC (UK), DfT (UK), DfE (UK), Ofgem (UK), BIT (UK)","diagram")]),
