q("T-C02","test","chart","Figure 2.10 plots HDI against planetary-pressure values. What does its 2022-versus-1990 comparison indicate about pressure for a given HDI level?","In 2022, the average planetary pressure needed to sustain a given HDI level was lower than in 1990.",[(71,"In 2022 the average planetary pressure required to sustain any given HDI level were lower than in 1990 (figure 2.10)","chart")]),
q("T-C03","test","chart","In Figure 5.1, which period has the highest share of people who both support democracy and view leaders who may undermine it positively?","2017–2022, at about 52% on the vertical axis.",[(161,"Figure 5.1 ... 2017–2022 ... highest point","chart")]),
q("T-C04","test","chart","Figure S.1 compares the observed global HDI trajectory with the path projected from the 1999–2019 trend. How are they related after 2020?","The observed trajectory remains below the pre-2019 trend/projection.",[(18,"A permanent shift in the Human Development Index trajectory","chart")]),
q("T-C05","test","chart","In Figure 1.9, what two outcomes are plotted across HDI groups?","2022 planetary-pressure index and additional extreme-temperature days above the 1986–2005 average by end-century.",[(52,"Figure 1.9 ... Index of Planetary Pressures value, 2022 ... Number of additional extreme temperature days above ... average by end-century","chart")]),
q("T-M01","test","multi_hop","Using Table 1 and Table 7, report Switzerland's life expectancy at birth and its planetary-pressures-adjusted HDI (PHDI).","Life expectancy at birth was 84.3 years (Table 1); PHDI was 0.826 (Table 7).",[(288,"1 Switzerland 0.967 84.3","table"),(315,"1 Switzerland 0.967 0.826","table")]),
q("T-M02","test","multi_hop","Combine Table 3.1 with the Figure 3.1 vaccine timeline: what provision type does the report use for a scientific breakthrough, and how quickly was Covid-19 vaccine authorization compared with the usual timeline?","A scientific breakthrough is a best-shot public good; Covid-19 vaccine authorization was unprecedentedly fast, around one year versus a usual 10–11 years.",[(91,"Best-shot (for example, scientific breakthrough)","table"),(96,"Figure 3.1 Authorization for Covid-19 vaccines was unprecedentedly fast ... years","chart")]),
